========================================================================
Goldbach partitions of even numbers -- numerical experiment
========================================================================
Bound (largest even n tested) : 2,000,000  (primes sieved to 2,000,000)
Even values examined          : 999,999 (n = 4, 6, ..., 2,000,000)

[a] Any even n in range with NO representation found?
    NONE. Every even n in [4, 2,000,000] has at least one partition.

[b] Minimum partition count over the range
    min count            = 1  (attained at n = 4)
    first n with 1       = 4
    largest n with 1     = 12
    #(even n with count 1) = 4

[c] Maximum partition count over the range
    max count = 27988  (attained at n = 1981980)

[d] Average partition count over all even n in range
    average = 5987.2143

[e] Record-setting n (Goldbach comet band structure)
    distinct record holders up to 2,000,000: 182
    -- record holders with n in [0, 1,000]:
         n =         4   count = 1
         n =        10   count = 2
         n =        22   count = 3
         n =        34   count = 4
         n =        48   count = 5
         n =        60   count = 6
         n =        78   count = 7
         n =        84   count = 8
         n =        90   count = 9
