[f] Measured vs Hardy-Littlewood heuristic (order-of-magnitude only)
    score = 2 * C2 * n / (log n)^2 * prod_{p|n, p>2} (p-1)/(p-2)
             n    measured    HL score    ratio
         1,000          28        36.9    0.759
        10,000         127       207.5    0.612
       100,000         810      1328.2    0.610
     1,000,000       5,402      9223.3    0.586
     2,000,000       9,720     16726.1    0.581
    (heuristic asymptotic, not an exact formula; magnitude agreement only)

Reference values asserted exactly (FFT and direct scan):
    n =    4: 1  OK
    n =   10: 2  OK
    n =  100: 6  OK
    n = 1000: 28  OK
FFT-vs-direct cross-checks (exact):
    n =         4: 1  OK
    n =        10: 2  OK
    n =       100: 6  OK
    n =     1,000: 28  OK
    n =   123,456: 1452  OK
    n =   500,000: 3052  OK
    n =   999,998: 4206  OK
    n = 1,999,998: 21850  OK
    n = 2,000,000: 9720  OK

FINITE RANGE ONLY: the above verifies the counts for every even
n in [4, 2,000,000]. A finite verification is NOT a proof of the
Goldbach conjecture, which remains open.
